      "text": "\n\n# Release Plan: New Authentication Flow (v2)\n\n**Owner:** Platform/Auth Team  \n**Status:** Draft \u2014 pending security review sign-off  \n**Target date:** T+14 days from security review completion  \n**Affected services:** `auth-service`, `api-gateway`, `web-frontend`, `mobile-sdk`, `admin-portal`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nReplace the legacy session-cookie auth flow with the new token-based flow (short-lived access tokens + rotating refresh tokens, PKCE for OAuth2, step-up MFA for sensitive actions). The legacy flow remains available behind a flag during the migration window.\n\n**Out of scope:** SSO/IdP integrations (separate epic), password reset UX redesign, mobile biometric enrollment (follow-up).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Feature Flags\n\n| Flag | Scope | Default | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `auth.v2.enabled` | Per-tenant (DB) | `false` | Master switch for new flow |\n| `auth.v2.mfa.stepup` | Per-tenant | `false` | Enable step-up MFA on sensitive endpoints |\n| `auth.v2.refresh.rotation` | Global (config) | `true` | Refresh token rotation on |\n| `auth.legacy.cookie.fallback` | Global (config) | `true` | Allow legacy cookie auth as fallback |\n| `auth.v2.debug.verbose` | Per-user (dev only) | `false` | Verbose auth logging (never in prod) |\n\n**Flag management:** All flags live in the existing `feature-flags` service. No hardcoded flags in application code. Flags are evaluated at the `api-gateway` edge and propagated via request context.\n\n**Kill switch:** Setting `auth.v2.enabled = false` for all tenants + `auth.legacy.cookie.fallback = true` reverts to legacy flow within one config push cycle (~30s).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Security Review\n\n**Must complete before any staging deployment.**\n\n- [ ] **Threat model review** \u2014 Auth team + Security team walk through the new token lifecycle, refresh rotation, and MFA step-up paths. Document in `docs/security/auth-v2-threat-model.md`.\n- [ ] **Token format & entropy audit** \u2014 Confirm access tokens are \u2265 256-bit random, refresh tokens are opaque (not JWT), and both are stored",
      "text_preview": "\n\n# Release Plan: New Authentication Flow (v2)\n\n**Owner:** Platform/Auth Team  \n**Status:** Draft \u2014 pending security review sign-off  \n**Target date:** T+14 days from security review completion  \n**Affected services:** `auth-service`, `api-gateway`, `web-frontend`, `mobile-sdk`, `admin-portal`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nReplac",
